   "text": "This structure is elvitegravir, a 4-quinolone-3-carboxylic acid.\n\n- **Quinolone core:** the ring nitrogen carries the side chain, C3 carries the COOH, and C4 is the C=O.\n- **Benzene ring of the quinolone:** it bears the OMe and the benzyl CH2 substituent.\n- **Benzyl group:** the CH2 is attached to an aryl ring with F ortho to the CH2 and Cl beside the F (a 3-chloro-2-fluorophenyl).\n- **N-substituent:** a CH bearing an isopropyl group and a CH2OH. The CH2OH is drawn on a hashed bond, so this carbon is the only stereocentre.\n\nFor the stereocentre, the priorities are N > CH2OH > iPr > H. With the CH2OH hashed, the implicit H points toward the viewer. From the front, N, CH2OH and iPr run clockwise, so with H pointing away the sense is reversed and the centre is S. In the SMILES below, `[C@@H]` written as iPr, H, CH2OH, N also gives S.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)[C@@H](CO)n1cc(C(=O)O)c(=O)c2cc(Cc3cccc(Cl)c3F)c(OC)cc12"
